  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The cubic unit cell structure of a compound containing cation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and anion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is shown below. When compared to the anion, the cation has smaller ionic radius. Choose the correct statement(s).\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/354372e2-04a1-477f-a885-42e90ebde8a5-image.png\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lWfl5",
      "text": "The empirical formula of the compound is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MX</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4Azc4",
      "text": "The cation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and anion<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&nbsp;have different coordination geometries.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eR7pz",
      "text": "The ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> bond length to the cubic unit cell edge length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>866</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OVgx3",
      "text": "The ratio of the ionic radii of cation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> to anion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>414</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>MX</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>732</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>866</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>-</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>732</mn></math></p>",
